  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nNo tricks, just treats are found in this forecast for the \ncoming days. High pressure building in from the west will settle\nin overhead today into tonight before gradually shifting off to\nour east early next week, resulting in another extended stretch\nof dry weather. Clouds around early this morning are expected \nto scatter out for some sunshine. Northwesterly flow in place \nwill lead to seasonably cool conditions this afternoon with \nhighs in the 50s along with less wind in comparison to \nyesterday. As trick-or-treating time starts to roll around early\nthis evening, temperatures will likely range from the upper 40s\nto the mid 50s around 5PM and fall into the 40s areawide by \n7-8PM. With light winds and high pressure overhead it will be \nchillier overnight with lows in the mid 20s to the mid 30s. \n\nAs the high starts to shift slowly east Sunday, the flow will \ngradually turn more westerly aloft and temperatures moderate a \nbit with highs in the upper 50s to lower 60s. A warming trend \ncontinues Monday through Wednesday with upper-level ridging \nbuilding in aloft and the flow becoming more south-\nsouthwesterly. Afternoon highs early next week will be running \nwell above average in the 60s with some valley locations even \nmaking a run at 70 degrees Tuesday and Wednesday. The next \nopportunity for more meaningful rainfall looks to be later \nWednesday night into Thursday as a frontal boundary approaches.",
